PROFESSIONAL SUMMARY
Software engineer focused on systems and full-stack development, with hands-on experience building
Rust infrastructure and TypeScript/Next.js applications. Designed a domain-agnostic Rust platform and
an indexing engine, with experience spanning runtime/lifecycle systems, reliability, real-time data
pipelines, backend APIs, and Al-enabled products.

ENGINEERING EXPERIENCE
Nizaam Islamic Ecosystem | Founder & Systems Engineer
Rust | Systems Engineering | Infrastructure | Indexing | Testing | Open Source
github.com/nizaam-islamic-ecosystem
September 2026 – Present
• Designed and implemented Nizaam Core, a domain-agnostic Rust infrastructure layer: typed contracts
and identities, runtime/lifecycle, transport and message framing, security boundaries, observability,
retry/idempotency, internal events, and a Control Plane.
• Built the Nizaam Indexing Engine on top of Core: index versioning, query planning and retrieval,
build/update/rebuild/publication workflows, integrity validation, capacity accounting, and durable
execution with recovery.
• Validated Core with 2,311 passing tests (1,576 unit, 735 integration) and zero failures, including
conformance, fault-injection, and stress suites; the Indexing Engine includes 992 test functions.
• Published nizaam-core v1.0.1 and nizaam-indexing v1.0.0 on crates.io (MIT); now developing further
engines on top of Core.

